WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.969
-Michael, I want
to keep the interview going,

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.037
but I thought we'd make the
conversation a little bit more

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.739
interesting with a game
we call "Word Sneak."

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.208
Here we go.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.209
-♪ Word Sneak, Word Sneak ♪

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.577
-Here's how it works.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.347
We each have cards with
random words written on them,

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.316
and our goal is to work these
words into the conversation

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:20.453
as casually and seamlessly
as possible.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.654
Make sense?

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.289
-Got it. Okay, okay, okay.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.624
-All right, so, now,
you look at your top card.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.792
I'll look at mine.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.294
You start it off
and let the Word Sneak begin.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.463 line:0%
Michael, any plans
for the summer?

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.333 line:0%
-Uh, the summer? Yeah.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.802 line:0%
You know,
I love getting outdoors.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.837 line:0%
You've been to Venice Beach?

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.506 line:0%
You know, they have the bicycles
and, like, the Rollerblades.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:41.941 line:0%
-Oh, yeah. I love Venice Beach.
-[ Bell dings ]

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.477 line:0%
-You know, outside -- You just
kind of like -- you just --

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.713 line:0%
-Yeah, and do you go right home
when you go from the beach?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:50.750 line:0%
You go right into your house?
-Uh, no, no.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.953 line:0%
Actually, you know,
I need to drive,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.989 line:0%
but sometimes, like,
the 405 is so packed.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.892 line:0%
You know, I mean,
there's like boats, tugboats,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.693 line:0%
and things like that.
I just kind of try to --

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.129 line:0%
-[ Bell dings ]
-You snuck in your word already.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.064 line:0%
I was just saying,
if you go to your house,

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.933 line:0%
there's probably sand
all over the place,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.068 line:0%
so you got to get a Roomba
to clean it up.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.370 line:0%
-[ Bell dings ]
-But it's no big deal.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.438 line:0%
-Oh, okay.
-But, I mean, that's good.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:16.409 line:0%
So you do that. Then --
And then you go on the 405.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.410 line:0%
You know what I like to do
when I used to drive?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.480 line:0%
I used to --
-Yeah.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.682 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.017 line:0%
-Used to get a little nervous.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.186 line:0%
Get a little nervous
before I'd drive, so...

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.587 line:0%
-Really?

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.757 line:0%
-Yeah, but my grandpa
told me a little trick.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:34.127 line:0%
Throw down a couple of
appletinis before you --

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.494 line:0%
-[ Bell dings ]
-Really?

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:37.930 line:0%
-Make sure you don't drive
too fast, of course, yeah.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.532 line:0%
-See, that's crazy
that he told you the appletinis.

00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:46.005 line:0%
For me, you know, I'm a eater.
You know, I eat, so --

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.775 line:0%
What really, like, settles
my stomach and my nerves

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.879 line:0%
when I do drive is --
You know, it's crazy.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.348 line:0%
Sometimes refried beans.
And, like, you know --

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.849 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.352 line:0%
-Wow. Refried beans is what
calms your nerves down?

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.588 line:0%
-Yeah. You know, with nachos.

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.122 line:0%
You know what I'm saying?
I like nachos.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.258 line:0%
Sometimes you got to put
the layer of refried beans.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.459 line:0%
-I can't eat that stuff.
I can't eat that stuff

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:12.065 line:0%
'cause I blow up
like a medium-sized ostrich.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.599 line:0%
-[ Bell dings ]
-People are like --

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:14.834 line:0%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.102 line:0%
Medium --
-Okay.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.104 line:0%
-You know, so I can't do
that type of stuff anymore.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:23.142 line:0%
-And then, you know, if you blow
up like a medium-sized ostrich,

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.977 line:0%
you know,
the nachos that I usually --

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:29.281 line:0%
You know, sometimes you might
chew on something crazy

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.617 line:0%
and, you know --
-I guess. I guess.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.753 line:0%
-The teeth.
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.322 line:0%
Like, sometimes your tooth's
all -- You're crazy.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.324 line:0%
Like, my dentist actually
stopped seeing me,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.527 line:0%
and I had to go see
John Cena's dentist.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:42.695 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.430 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.298 line:0%
Yeah, I had to go
see him one time.

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:47.667 line:0%
-Wow.
-He took me in last-minute.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.435 line:0%
It was great. It was great.
It was great.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.204 line:0%
-John Cena's dentist?
-Yeah.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.205 line:0%
-Yeah, and that's interesting
'cause he --

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.607 line:0%
The dentist actually says,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.676 line:0%
"You can't see me,"
as he's operating on you.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.745 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
I see what you did.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.548 line:0%
-I know that dentist,
'cause I went to this weird

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:06.352 line:0%
party a couple years ago,
and I ended up in a hot tub

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.488 line:0%
with John Cena's dentist --
was in there.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.022 line:0%
-Okay.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.824 line:0%
-Crazy.
A lot of people in there.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.126 line:0%
Cindy Adams was in there.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:17.163 line:0%
Biv from Bell Biv Devoe
was in there.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.998 line:0%
-Hmm.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.167 line:0%
Could've been Bell.
I think it was Biv, though.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.502 line:0%
Biv was there.
-Okay, okay.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:27.507 line:0%
-This dude who played bass for
one of Brian McKnight's tours.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:31.844 line:0%
-Okay.
-Uh, uh, uh, the dude that --

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.879 line:0%
who drew Scooter --
he did the voice of Scooter

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.417 line:0%
from "Muppet Babies."
He was in there.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.452 line:0%
Just a bunch -- The kid from
"Jerry Maguire" was in there.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.853 line:0%
-Wait. How big was --
-[ Bell dings ]

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.054 line:0%
-Really?
-Yeah, it was just --

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:43.756 line:0%
I had to get
the hell out of there.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.958 line:0%
-I mean, what kind of --
That's a big hot tub.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.827 line:0%
-It was a small pool.
It was a small pool.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.795 line:0%
-Small pool.
-But all those people in there

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:53.098 line:0%
at once made it hot, you know?
-Gotcha.

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:55.902 line:0%
-Yeah, heated it right up.
-Yes, yes, yes. Yes.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:04:00.539 line:0%
-Yeah. You ever been to, like,
a crazy party or something?

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.174 line:0%
-Yeah. You know what?

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:05.311 line:0%
I'm more of a --
I'm a homebody, you know?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.745 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.915 line:0%
-And I --
Sometimes I pick up hobbies.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.316 line:0%
You know, like,
I don't know, guitar or --

00:04:11.316 --> 00:04:13.552 line:0%
You know,
tattooing was something

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:16.021 line:0%
that I was interested in
at one point.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.191 line:0%
-Wow.
That's an interesting hobby.

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.992 line:0%
-Sometimes I do random
piercings, you know,

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.627 line:0%
lip piercings
and stuff like that.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.796 line:0%
If you wanted it, I could,
like, give you a lip ring.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.598 line:0%
You know, I could do that.
-[ Bell dings ]

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.566 line:0%
-You could.
-If you were into it.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:31.237 line:0%
-[As Elmer Fudd] I'm weally,
weally scared of that.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.940 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.508 line:0%
I'm weall-- I'm --

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:38.677 line:0%
That's scare-wee.
Weally scare-wee.

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.746 line:0%
-That sounds like --
What is that?

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.915 line:0%
Was that --
That sounds like Bugs Bunny.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.350 line:0%
-Oh, you wascally wabbit.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.618 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.852 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.954 line:0%
[Normal voice] That's my man.
He set me up.

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.691 line:0%
Michael B. Jordan!
That's my man right there!

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.826 line:0%
His new movie,
"Without Remorse,"

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:57.263 line:0%
is available tomorrow
on Amazon Prime Video.

